    "description": "Family of digital indicators (A-Series and V-Series) connected to a weighing platform forming a Class III or IIII, mains or battery-powered, self-indicating, single interval or dual interval/range, non-automatic weighing instrument; may be used for direct sales to the public. Stainless steel enclosure (AFS, APS, VFS, VPS) or plastic enclosure (AFM, ATM, ABM, VFM, VBM, VTM); 2.0-inch graphic LCD (1.0-inch on APS and VPS); A/D conversion module and main board with processor. Devices include initial and semi-automatic zero setting, zero tracking, semi-automatic subtractive tare balancing, determination of stability of equilibrium, zero indicator, net indicator, memory and totalisation, and printing. Load cells must have an OIML R60 Certificate of Conformity with the necessary data for the manufacturer's declaration of compatibility; load cells marked NH are allowed only if humidity testing to R76 was conducted on them; compatibility of load cell and indicator is established via the compatibility of modules calculation at verification. Legally relevant parameters protected by a jumper on the main board; enclosures and load cell connection sealed using a wire-and-seal method."
